@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "How we handle location data";
}

<div class="page page-narrow">
    <p class="kicker">Privacy</p>
    <h1 style="font-size: 2rem;">How we handle location data</h1>

    <p>
        When you report a break-in, you place a pin at (or type in) the spot
        where it happened. We store that precise point privately, but it is
        <strong>never</strong> shown publicly and never returned by any page
        or API on this site.
    </p>
    <p>
        What the map actually displays is that point snapped to roughly the
        block level — close enough to see the pattern across a neighborhood,
        not precise enough to point at a specific house or tell anyone which
        driveway a car was parked in.
    </p>
    <p>
        Reports are anonymous. We don't collect names, emails, or accounts.
        If you upload a photo, make sure it doesn't show anything that could
        identify you or your address before submitting it.
    </p>
</div>
